Dear list,

I am currently using DISTANCE to analyse line transects of herbivores on =
savannah plains. My problem is that many species occur in mixed =
clusters. For example, a cluster may consist of 50 individuals of =
species A and 2 of species B. If I am calculating abundance of species B =
I have a problem determining the cluster size - the effective cluster =
size is 52, the actual number of animals is 2. If I use 2 then analysis =
of the cluster size/distance relationship will be wrong as small =
clusters would occasionally be visible at large distances because they =
are part of large, mixed clusters, but if I use 52 the actual number of =
animals is wrong. Does anyone know of a way of seperating effective and =
actual cluster sizes?

My thanks in advance,

Tom Maddox,
Institute of Zoology
London

