Dear list,

I am having problems using the post stratification option to investigate =
differences between repeat surveys apparantly because I did not repeat =
every transect on every survey round, yet the post stratification option =
appears to assume I did. For example, my survey consisted of 16 =
different 5km line transects surveyed across 8 months. In month 1 I =
completed all transects. In month 2 I repeated 14 of these but could not =
complete the other 2. In month 3 I completed 12, 14 in month 4 etc. =
Across 8 surveys I should have theoretically collected data for =
16x8=3D128 transects across 128x5=3D640 kms but in fact I collected 110 =
transects across 550 km. The file is set up with the time period (month) =
as an observation layer:

Stratum | Transect label | Transect length | Month | Perp. Distance

and post stratification is carried out on month. Before stratification =
the results appear ok - sample size is 16. However, after post =
stratification the results show a sample size of 128 kms and effort of =
640 kms even though I have only entered data for 110 transects across =
550 km! Obviously this causes the density estimates to be wrong. I have =
tried entering dummy values for missing transects with distance=3D0 but =
the analysis does not accept these. Does anyone know if this is a =
problem with my data format, the fact I have missed transects or my =
analysis method and more importantly, how to solve it?

Many thanks,

Tom Maddox

